    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d521">

                <pb facs="0782" n="768" sameAs="frus:frus1946v06/pg768"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20211/7–1846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-18">July 18, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1312. Sov. Navy Lieut. Nicolai Redin acquitted July 17 by US Federal Court jury
                    on espionage and conspiracy charges. Further info re trial and newspaper reports
                    will be forwarded Emb.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d521-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d521-f1" n="19" xml:id="d521-f1-content">
                <p>Further information and newspaper clippings were enclosed in instruction 1296,
                    July 26, 1946, to Moscow, not printed. Redin’s trial was held in Seattle before
                    Federal District Judge Lloyd Black. On July 17, the jury acquitted Redin on all
                    charges. According to newspaper reports he expressed his thanks for a fair
                    trial.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
